  Item_133477_Desc = {
    Text = "The clinking of iron chains echoed through the empty dungeon.\nWith her only working hand, the girl dragged her broken body, inching slowly toward the pitch-black slime.\nHere, the only witnesses were the mounds of bones piled in the corner.\nShe didn't care whether she'd end up like them. She only knew how much people feared that power.\n\n\"At least... it can't be worse than this...\"\n\nThe slime crept upward along her slender index finger and swallowed her whole in an instant.\nIt began to churn and boil. It writhed with a frenzied joy, as if it had finally found its destined vessel.\nAfter a long while, silence returned to the cell. Twisted hands pierced through the cocoon of slime, tearing open the last shell that had ever kept her from the world.\nThe girl gazed calmly at her limbs, now mutated into oozing black slime. The chains binding her wrists and neck shattered effortlessly against this new power. For the first time, she felt truly unburdened.\nShe breathed in the prison air greedily. The stench of rotting corpses and filth surrounded her, but she did not care.\nFor she had finally tasted it—the thing she had dreamed of since birth:\n<Italic:Freedom.>\nThe cage was broken. The goddess of vengeance bared her claws, turning her wrath upon all who had enslaved her.\n...\nPeople screamed.\n\"H-help! This slave's gone mad! Guards! Where are the guards?!\"\nPeople begged.\n\"Don't kill me! Please, let me go... I—I’ll give you all my money!\"\nPeople fled.\n\"The King is dead! Run, run for your lives! She's not human... she's a monster!\"\nPeople fell silent.\n\"...Ngh... Ugh...\"\n...\nThe slaughter ceased. She casually tossed aside a head without a glance—a face frozen in the grimace of suffocation, airway clogged, life choked out.\nWith her fury spent, she began to wonder: <Italic:what now?>\nThe wind swept through the corpse-littered city-state, carrying sludge and blood to smear the ruins in wanton strokes.\nFinally, the girl took a step forward.\nShe would live as a warrior—restless, unyielding—to sow the seeds of freedom.\nShe would journey north, all the way to the ends of the polar ice."
  },
