  },
  Item_140416_Desc = {
    Text = [[
"The soul serves as the instrument, echoing the cosmos.
Through chaos, dissonance, frenzied rhythm, this concerto resounds to unveil the world's ultimate truth."]]
  },
  Item_140416_Name = {
    Text = "Concerto of Dissonance"
  },
  Item_140416_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "V2.5.1 Avatar Bundle"
  },
  Item_140417_Desc = {
    Text = "The first movement, begins. Before his raised hands descend into stillness, the entire universe resounds with the sonata of endings."
  },
  Item_140417_Name = {
    Text = "Celestial Accord"
  },
  Item_140418_Desc = {
    Text = "\"Where petals weep crimson, flame forges them into a final verse. Elegance, romance, and tears that fall without a sound.\""
  },
  Item_140418_Name = {
    Text = "The Rose's Psalm"
  },
  Item_140418_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "V2.5.1 Avatar Bundle"
  },
  Item_140459_Desc = {
    Text = "Before the baton was raised, the world was a cacophony of loathsome noise.\nThe heavy thud of his father's palm striking the piano lid; the whispers of sycophants drifting through the palace corridors; the endless chatter about him filling the newspapers.\n\"Silence.\"\n@3 Royal Opera House, Spring of @36.\nThe young court musician stepped onto the chief conductor's podium for the first time. Among the audience, skepticism and anticipation echoed with equal fervor. He was so young, so taciturn, with his brilliant talent sealed within him—like a piece of fine porcelain that had never been permitted to see the light of day. Now, for the first time, he raised his baton upon the crimson stage.\nThe moment the baton rose, the theater's very air was seized by an unseen force. It was the pull of gravity, the tide's inexorable draw—an axiom beyond defiance in the cosmos of music.\nThe baton fell. The notes tore through the velvet veil of silence; the bow of the concertmaster trembled slightly. He had long since forgotten that the figure before him was a mere child, fifty years his junior. The arc of the baton guided him onward; his fingers were no longer entirely his to command.\nStrings surged, brass resonated, and the timpani erupted at the precise, destined moment. Every section was reined in by invisible threads, surrendering to the elegant arcs traced above the podium.\nHamlin's lips drew into a cold, thin line; his pale, youthful face was so exquisite it seemed unreal. Every sweep of his baton carried an unassailable decree. From the very first moment he gripped that baton, he knew with absolute clarity: Music is never performed; it is ruled.\nAs the movement reached its cadenza, Hamlin's gaze swept over the musicians—they were now little more than marionettes to him. His eyes held no one. On the stage of music, he was the sole autocrat.\nThe finale. The last note dissolved into stillness. After a prolonged silence, applause broke over the hall like a rising tide.\nThat day, the headlines belonged to Hamlin alone. The young genius had claimed accolades and adoration unmatched by any before him. Yet, facing the first frenzied ovation of his life, the young conductor did not show the slightest trace of a smile.\nHe bowed, slowly lowered his baton. He left the first stage he had ever stood upon, declined the palace banquet, and returned to his practice room.\nMediocre players, imprecise vibratos, a breath misplaced by an eighth of a beat—every flaw was a profanation of music. Amidst the thunderous cheers, he heard the one true sound: behind the unreachable dome above him, something was tolling for him. It called to him, chastised him, and waited for him. They were destined to meet. And when that moment came, he would have to be flawless.\nThat day, the demon maestro's overture conquered his first stage.\nBut the grand, unending movement toward the divine had only just begun to unfold."
  },
  Item_140459_Name = {
    Text = "Ouvertüre Universell"
  },
