  },
  Item_68682_Name = {
    Text = "Blue Stone Throne"
  },
  Item_68682_StoryDesc = {
    Text = [[
In the endless abyss, the Azure Throne stands sentinel,
The sky hangs low, the stars tremble, and all creation is silent.

Ancient and mysterious entities have been utterly annihilated,
Yet across generations, mortals chant their hymns in dreams.
The abyssal waters and secrets long sealed in dust,
Your whispers surge like a tide, drowning the ravines of the soul.

In that boundless dreamscape, the Prophet and the Madman walk together,
In pursuit of the intangible spirit, fear and reverence intertwined.
The path entangled with dark algae, like a destiny being spun,
Gradually drawing the hearts of the lost toward that Azure Throne.
Ah, the universe's absurdity and its truth,
Where dream and reality intersect, an eternal brilliance flickers.]]
  },
  Item_68683_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with the DMG Amplification attribute."
  },
  Item_68683_Name = {
    Text = "Witch's Wide-brimmed Hat"
  },
  Item_68683_StoryDesc = {
    Text = [[
The connection between the witch and the wide-brimmed hat is sometimes like the relationship between the chicken and the egg; it's hard to distinguish whether the hat made the witch or the witch made the hat.
But anyway, Daffodil possesses such an elegant wide-brimmed hat.
This hat originally belonged to the former shopkeeper, back when Daffodil's name did not yet belong to her. She was merely a confused ghost, subdued and bewildered, like an ignorant beast.
The woman who always smiled took her, patiently teaching her, as one would teach a child, little by little, how to be a "person," and the secrets to interacting with others.
The bustling port city gathered the richest crystallizations of human culture at that time. The street where the exchange shop is located featured a plethora of shops, covering a vast array of items, and the shopkeeper always seemed to chat with all the shop owners as if they were old friends.
"She's really amazing," Daffodil thought back then, "but it's not strange; no one could dislike her."
The shopkeeper enjoyed shopping, so for the first time in millennia, Daffodil, who had always played the part of a human whose head she had severed, was asked to give her opinion.
"Which one do you think looks better? This little top hat or this wide-brimmed hat?"
The woman tried on an array of dazzling hats in front of the mirror. To Daffodil, they were merely props to wrap her body and make herself look more human.
But that day, as she watched the shopkeeper wearing the wide-brimmed hat like a giant flower on her head, an image suddenly emerged in her mind of the woman wearing such a hat, and the two of them strolling on the beach.
"This one," she suddenly said, "just this one."
The shopkeeper turned back in surprise, as if she hadn't expected Daffodil to express her preferences so clearly.
"Alright, it is indeed a beautiful hat. Since you chose it for me, I will cherish it well."
Whether it was to encourage Daffodil or not, this hat, just as the shopkeeper promised, became a permanent adornment on her head until the final moment when it was handed over to Daffodil by the shopkeeper, along with her smiling head.
"What a lovely hat, I will definitely cherish it well."
The gorgeous purple-black flowers finally bloomed on the new owner's head.]]
  },
  Item_68688_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with the Keyflare Regen Level attribute."
  },
  Item_68688_Name = {
    Text = "Genesis Tulu SR (Suggested Translation)"
  },
  Item_68688_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "Genesis Tulu SR (Suggested Translation)"
  },
  Item_68689_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with the Keyflare Regen Level attribute."
  },
  Item_68689_Name = {
    Text = "Hypnotic Pendulum"
  },
  Item_68689_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "The reborn Clementine is like a naive larva, traveling through the human world, wandering in the prosperous world that does not belong to her race, feeling perplexed and confused.\nUntil that enlightening voice rings out—\n\"Excuse me, are you Doctor Charlotte? I came to seek psychological counseling from Doctor Charlotte...\"\nClementine finally comes to her senses. She doesn't care who Charlotte is; she is simply curious about the new term that the visitor spoke: \"psychological counseling\".\nBut she is a mature hunter and will never reveal her ignorance, so she smiled, as if she were Charlotte, the savior spoken of by the visitor.\nTears, torment, helplessness, no need to provoke; the visitor has already squeezed out the pain from the depths of her soul.\nBefore leaving, the visitor looked at Clementine with a relaxed expression and sighed, \"Thank you for being willing to listen. I feel so much better.\"\nThen came the sound of the door closing, along with Clementine's laughter, as she tasted the sweetness for the first time.\nThis laughter started softly, like that of a larva's buzzing, and then grew louder, as if it was the screech of an adult insect.\nAnd in this laughter, the insectoid named Clementine swiftly matured.\nEverything that followed fell into place. She became a psychologist, carrying a smile and a pendulum, diving deep into each patient's heart.\nShe continues to walk through the world of humans, still not belonging to this prosperous world, but no longer confused and perplexed.\nFor the entire human world is her hypnotic hunting ground."
  },
