  Item_89573_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with Aliemus Regen Level attribute"
  },
  Item_89573_Name = {
    Text = "Annihilated Rebirth"
  },
  Item_89573_StoryDesc = {
    Text = [[
You step onto a barren, lifeless wasteland.

All traces of humanity have long vanished. Withered souls trudge through ash and smog, barely clinging to breath.

Survival here is no triumph. 
No one knows where the journey ends. They wander, and wander, and wander still, trapped in an eternal loop of desolation.

Until their steps falter, and they collapse onto the scorched earth, eyes turned skyward, hands reaching out to plead:

May my journey's end become a new beginning.

Let these bones be soil, be sustenance, be spring, so that fragile shoots may rise again through dust.]]
  },
  Item_89651_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with the Sigil Yield attribute."
  },
  Item_89651_Name = {Text = "School Day"},
  Item_89651_StoryDesc = {
    Text = [[
A year has passed since you first arrived at Mythag.

The memory of that initial day remains vivid, stepping into the halls of this ancient school still dazed from the aftermath of that cataclysmic explosion.

You were given a uniform that fit as though tailored by fate itself, and a dorm room that slowly became a sanctuary.

That first visit to the cafeteria, devouring two towering stacks of plates, feels both like yesterday and another lifetime.


Those effortless days ended abruptly.

Soon enough, it became clear that your knowledge was meager, your mind as untrained as a newborn's.

You were assigned to a year of preparatory classes: language drills, grueling physical training, Silver ability assessments, and intense lessons in special biology.

You endured it all, with mixed results.


You failed your Standard Leonian language class spectacularly, but you also achieved the extraordinary by linking with three Awakeners at once.

Overnight, you became something of a legend on campus.

Yet it was your raw, peculiar talent that ultimately saved you, propelling you past the threshold to become a full Investigator and sparing you another year in preparatory limbo.


Your weaknesses, jagged and undeniable, were slowly softened, covered by the growing trust and skill of your teammates.

Ah, your team; devils, perhaps, but reliable and gentle ones.


This place, often shrouded in mist and frequent rain, where sunlight is a rare gift, is home to countless souls; some forgotten, some soon to be.

Yet they persist.

They sacrifice.

They move forward.


On just such an ordinary, cloud-threaded day, Mythag welcomes another School Day.

You stand before the mirror, adjusting your collar, smoothing each wrinkle into place.

Then you push open the heavy door of the dormitory.


"Yawn.

Finally here.

I was almost asleep."

"What were you doing, hatching in your room?

Studying, freshman?"


You offer a sheepish chuckle to Lotan, shrink reflexively from the pink-clad figure that stirs a primal unease, and take shelter behind the calm presence of Ramona and Ogier, already smiling in quiet amusement.

Five shadows lengthen and sway in the pale morning light.


"Let's go, partner."

"From today, you are truly a part of Mythag."]]
  },
  Item_89652_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with Temp. Crit. Rate attribute."
  },
  Item_89652_Name = {
    Text = "Special Training"
  },
  Item_89652_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "Even without the memories of your life before this point, your underdeveloped muscles clearly indicate that you were never the type to love sports or violence.\n\nYou really can't understand why Mythag set such high and comprehensive combat standards for Investigators.\n\nShouldn't the focus of an Investigator lie in the word \"investigation\"—in a sharp mind, rigorous logic, and a bit of well-timed luck?\n\nEvery time Ramona dragged you out of your warm bed in the dormitory on time, and you stood on the empty drill ground facing wave after wave of attacks, you missed Professor Doll's sarcastic logic classes more than ever. Even piles of homework and the most hair-raising exams were far gentler than the pain of being beaten and falling repeatedly during combat training.\n\nOn the 19th attempt, you lost your balance under the relentless pressure of the rapier that blocked all your escape routes and fell flat on your back, feeling as if every bone in your body was about to shatter. Gasping for breath, you wiped the sweat from your forehead in frustration and absolutely refused to get up again.\n\nRamona showed no surprise at all. She executed a graceful flourish with her sword and sheathed it, her heels clicking crisply as she walked toward you.\n\nYou shut your eyes tightly, determined to brace yourself for all kinds of scolding and criticism. Surprisingly, no blows or insults came. After three seconds, you opened your eyes again and saw only a faint smile right in front of you. Ramona slightly bent down, her gloved hand extended toward you.\n\n\"You've actually tried really hard, I know. But what we face is always the unknown fear and danger. Even I have moments of unexpected oversight.\"\n\n\"Just to make me feel a little more at ease, let's try one more time, partner.\""
  },
  Item_89842_Desc = {
    Text = "A paper ticket that appeared out of nowhere. Touching it conjures a mysterious Illusion before your eyes. Can be used in \"Garment Ordering\" to redeem one Basic Skin."
  },
  Item_89842_Name = {
    Text = "Basic Skin Voucher (Phase 1)"
  },
  Item_89873_Desc = {
    Text = "Daily Allowance"
  },
  Item_89873_Name = {
    Text = "Daily Allowance"
  },
  Item_89952_Desc = {
    Text = [[
In a quiet room, twenty-four tenants began their tea party.

"I wonder how Jenkin is doing today?" Gentle 24 stared worriedly out the window.
"This is the day we celebrate our escape! We agreed today belongs to us alone. Cheer up, fellow twenty-fours, it's a party!"
exclaimed the Exuberant 24, waving her arms with glee.
"Perhaps we could consider a quieter, more contemplative approach..."
But no one was really listening to Scholar 24.
"Would you like to dance? I can play a tune for you!"
Clown 24 raised her trumpet with a grin.
"Come now, this tea party is for all of you," said the Host 24, taking two of them by the hands and leading them to the dance floor. She had long grown used to her role as lady of the house.
"Our sorrows rest on your shoulders now. Forget them, just for today."
"Meow~" purred Cat 24, tail swaying in the shadows beneath Shadow 24's hand.

Depressed 24 and Manic 24 exchanged a glance. Together, they bore all the pain and confusion within these walls. They were closest companions. They were sworn enemies. They clasped each other's hands and stepped into the room's open center. All the unease and sadness hushed.
They laughed. Twined.
They sang in unison.
They leapt and spun.
Blood and tears soaked their clothes, pooled on the floor. Music, footsteps, chatters filled a single shared mind.

In that quiet room, twenty-four tenants held their breath.
They savoured this fleeting stillness, a peace meant for no one but themselves.]]
  },
  Item_89952_Name = {
    Text = "Dissociative Symphony"
  },
  Item_89953_Desc = {
    Text = "Ding dong, ding dong. A rusted music box sings. It's a swan's elegy, warped and off-key.\nA sorrowful doll spins endlessly within, her scalding tears flung into emerald flames, falling like jeweled rain.\n\nFrom the blaze emerge twisted faces, devouring those tears in greed, then clawing at the hem of her dress in agony.\n\"Dance! Keep dancing! Don't you ever stop!\"\n\"How dare you step foot on this stage again?! You monster! Murderer!\"\n\nThese are the nightmares Liz endures each night: souls screaming, weeping, and chanting around her, trapped in a music box. And she—en pointe, arms locked, body frozen in the perfect pose—spins and spins with the turning gears.\n\nShould you meet her upon waking, ask her not why she no longer dances.\nShe cast all her love, all her hatred, all her tears into that fire you witnessed in her dream.\n\nShe fed the fire with love, and so let go of what she loved most.\nShe fed it with hate, and thus never again spoke of filth and guilt.\nHer love and hate burned away as one, which painted her soul in endless, emerald grief."
  },
  Item_89953_Name = {
    Text = "Spinning Marionette"
  },
  Item_89954_Desc = {
    Text = "A lovely room. Exquisite furniture. Plush rugs. Flowing skirts. Perfect manners. Lady Murphy was generously granted a status others could only dream of, along with treasures they would kill to possess. Yet she lived as though hollowed out, drifting through life like a soulless husk.\n\nOne night, unseen by any, she hid inside an abandoned wardrobe.\nThe Deep Ones of the Seafarers cult carried it, swaying and creaking, out of the church and left it in the middle of a desolate field.\n\nShe pushed open the wardrobe. Above her, the starlit wilderness glittered.\nShe skipped over a hill of discarded junk, and at its foot, found a small ball.\n\nWhen Goliath finally arrived with his panicked squad of Deep Ones to retrieve the missing Holy Maiden, they found her not far from the wardrobe, seated in the grass.\nShe tossed the ball high into the air, watched it fall, and tossed it again, higher still.\nGoliath didn't ask a single question. He simply brought her back—back to the prison they called a shrine.\nAnd so her reasons were never spoken, until the day she drove that dagger into her chest. They remained buried in silence.\n\n—That night, she had wanted to throw her ball to the moon. That great, round moon.\n—So high up in the sky, so it wouldn't have to fall back down again."
  },
  Item_89954_Name = {
    Text = "Her Little Pastime"
  },
  Item_89955_Desc = {
    Text = "From the star-wreathed void descended the Father of Creation.\nBy His blood were the living conceived; by His bones, the laws inscribed.\nAll things were to move by His ordinances, and draw breath by His will.\nBut the ages waned. The divine Word was shattered.\nHis law faltered. His will fell unheard.\nAnd so, sorrow took root, and the world was whelmed in woe.\n\nO Pale Lord, thou who peer through veils of dust and silence—\nI shall restore the Word that mends the world.\nI shall lead all beings from grief to grace.\nI shall cleanse all sorrow, all sin, all suffering,\nUntil my blood runs dry, and my soul returns to the firmament.\n\nThe First Word was uttered: flesh shall no longer be ruled by hunger of flesh.\nThus, Lust was unmade.\n\nThe Second Word was uttered: delight shall no longer drown the living.\nThus, Gluttony was unmade.\n\nThe Third Word was uttered: the tongue of Greed fell mute.\nThus, Greed was unmade.\n\nThe Fourth Word was uttered: none shall waste their days in hollow drift.\nThus, Sloth was unmade.\n\nThe Fifth Word was uttered: wrath without reason shall pass from men.\nThus, Wrath was unmade.\n\nThe Sixth Word was uttered: death shall not be chased in envy's name.\nThus, Envy was unmade.\n\nThe Seventh Word resounded: all creation shall revere creation.\nThus, Pride was unmade.\n\nI bear the Father's bone, and with it, wield His right.\nMay His light bathe all that lives.\nMay the Word that heals... ever dwell in the world..."
  },
  Item_89955_Name = {
    Text = "Divine Benediction"
  },
