  Item_91121_Desc = {
    Text = "As many people admired her decisiveness and courage back then, just as many envy the fortune of such a rebirth.\nHer active mind commands an endless supply of replaceable, bulletproof, and ageless bodies. The temptation of immortality, like an eternal forbidden fruit and a beacon of light, draws in those who have already attained wealth and power.\nThere was once a prominent figure that even Mythag couldn't refuse, who offered an extremely generous set of terms in exchange for Doll performing the same brain transplant surgery and awakening process for him. Doll did not refuse, nor did she mock his ignorance; she simply took a brief meeting out of her busy schedule to conduct a thorough examination. Then, she calmly announced a conclusion that enraged him—his brain did not meet the conditions for rebirth.\nWith Mythag's repeated mediation, the gravely ill and dying figure signed a series of exemption agreements, insisting on taking a gamble on that slim hope. Doll personally performed the surgery for him, but unfortunately, the hope had never existed.\nWhen Doll issued the negative verdict, that underdeveloped brain could never regain its original intellect. However, considering the generous compensation he had offered, Doll kindly completed the after-sales service: that brain, which had retained its vitality, was placed into a brain tank and equipped with a precisely matched system.\nThus, in Doll's laboratory, gradually appeared some small assistants that met the aesthetic tastes of the flying fungi. Those tiny creatures capable of brief flight waved their nimble legs, performing the simplest tasks and contributing to scientific research and progress.\n\"I03, fetch a new bottle of distilled water.\"\n\"I05, replace last week's culture medium.\" \"I01, help me brew a cup of coffee.\"\nIt seems an ignorant brain isn't entirely useless after all. Doll thought with a smile as the steam from her coffee rose gently."
  },
