  Item_91764_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Unlock after obtaining the skin "Bloodforged Diadem".
"I came. I saw. I slaughtered.."]]
  },
  Item_91764_Name = {
    Text = "Uvhash: Bloodforged Diadem"
  },
  Item_91765_Desc = {
    Text = "No matter how many years passed, he would never forget that era—the glorious, blood-drenched age of gladiators\n\"Uvhash...\"\nAt first, the slave owner who had paid a fortune for his flesh still needed to bellow his name to the crowd. But after he slaughtered his opponents, after his bare hands ripped out their steaming entrails and his teeth drank deep from their throats, the arena itself began chanting his titles.\n\"The Vampire,\" \"The Devil,\" \"Tyrant of the Arena\"...\nThe names shifted like desert sands as his opponents grew ever stronger—first trembling children, then seasoned warriors, then starved tigers and lions whose bones cracked like dry kindling beneath his hands.\nTo Uvhash, their dying words meant less than flies buzzing about corpses. He never remembered their pleas—\"What are you fighting for?\" Only one thing mattered. One simple act he repeated: slaughter. While he stood in the arena, he was its uncrowned king.\nAnd this simplicity granted him everything.\nPeople roared his name until Rome's greatest colosseum trembled. They showered him with so much gold that blood-stained sand vanished beneath coins. He cared not at all.\nThe cheers turned to ash in his ears; the wealth meant less than dirt. Only the warmth of fresh blood felt real. Only slaughter held meaning.\nFor his hunger demanded the simplest sacrament:\nI came. I saw. I slaughtered."
  },
  Item_91765_Name = {
    Text = "Bloodforged Diadem"
  },
  Item_91766_Desc = {
    Text = "In the lightless, endless labyrinth, a newcomer finally stumbled in—and Agrippa, the eternally bored Ashen Mistress, cracked her first genuine smile in forever.\n\"Choose,\" she whispered, \"you've got options here. Either pledge yourself to me and be reborn as my offspring, or try to starve in this maze... and become my offspring still.\"\nThe stranger's eyes dilated; their face contorted through waves of confusion, dawning horror, and animal panic—before they spun and fled, as countless others had before them.\n\"Ahhh? You elect to run~\" Her laughter slithered through the stones. \"Then run, little morsel! Run until your lungs bleed! As if you'll ever get out.\"\nWhat followed was the same routine she'd seen a thousand times: for her, it never gets old. The frantic sprint turning to exhausted stagger, the pathetic crawling, the muffled sobs. The darkness pressed in heavier with each step until their mind just... broke.\nOnly when they were properly wrecked did Agrippa materialize in front of them. The broken heap of a person didn't even look up, just weakly lifted a shaking hand.\n\"P-please... Anyone... Help...\"\nAgrippa crouched down with mock sympathy, her smile a sickle moon in the gloom. \"Of course I'll help. Just as your predecessors did... You need only become my child.\"\n\"Yesss,\" she crooned, \"the covenant will make all suffering go a way. Only a signature, and the pain stops.\"\nThe pathetic human nodded weakly, their eyes empty. And once more, in the labyrinth's eternal night, the Ashen Mistress smiled.\nThe ink dried. Now came the patient vigil... for her newest progeny to quicken in the dark."
  },
  Item_91766_Name = {
    Text = "Pallid Covenant"
  },
  Item_91767_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Unlocked after obtaining the Awakener Skin "Pallid Covenant."
"Sign the contract and become my progeny~"]]
  },
  Item_91767_Name = {
    Text = "Agrippa: Pallid Covenant"
  },
  Item_94417_Desc = {
    Text = "No matter how many years passed, he would never forget that era—the glorious, blood-drenched age of gladiators\n\"Uvhash...\"\nAt first, the slave owner who had paid a fortune for his flesh still needed to bellow his name to the crowd. But after he slaughtered his opponents, after his bare hands ripped out their steaming entrails and his teeth drank deep from their throats, the arena itself began chanting his titles.\n\"The Vampire,\" \"The Devil,\" \"Tyrant of the Arena\"...\nThe names shifted like desert sands as his opponents grew ever stronger—first trembling children, then seasoned warriors, then starved tigers and lions whose bones cracked like dry kindling beneath his hands.\nTo Uvhash, their dying words meant less than flies buzzing about corpses. He never remembered their pleas—\"What are you fighting for?\" Only one thing mattered. One simple act he repeated: slaughter. While he stood in the arena, he was its uncrowned king.\nAnd this simplicity granted him everything.\nPeople roared his name until Rome's greatest colosseum trembled. They showered him with so much gold that blood-stained sand vanished beneath coins. He cared not at all.\nThe cheers turned to ash in his ears; the wealth meant less than dirt. Only the warmth of fresh blood felt real. Only slaughter held meaning.\nFor his hunger demanded the simplest sacrament:\nI came. I saw. I slaughtered."
  },
  Item_94417_Name = {
