  Item_94440_Name = {Text = "Mouchette"},
  Item_94441_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The lost consciousness of an ancient will. Mythag enlightens the consciousness of Awakeners through a mysterious ritual, and the Enlightened Awakener will gain permanent enhancements.
Convert upon obtaining duplicate Mouchette. Activates Mouchette's Enlightens.]]
  },
  Item_94441_Name = {
    Text = "Shard: Mouchette"
  },
  Item_94441_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "Convert upon obtaining duplicate Mouchette. Activates Mouchette's Enlightens."
  },
  Item_94442_Desc = {
    Text = "Unlock after acquiring Awakener \"Genesis: Ogier\""
  },
  Item_94442_Name = {
    Text = "Genesis Ogier"
  },
  Item_94443_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with the Death Resistance attribute."
  },
  Item_94443_Name = {
    Text = "Light of Intellect"
  },
  Item_94443_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "With reason as a guiding light, one can dispel the mist of life.\n\nOnce upon a time, Mouchette had heard such words.\n\nPerhaps it was a technician from Thoreau Company casually expressing this sentiment while debugging a mist lamp?\nOr maybe it was a quip from a passerby during a visit to the Filingen restaurant?\n\nMouchette had forgotten; all she could clearly remember was the habitual social smile on her face when she heard those words, and the sarcasm hidden behind that smile.\n\n\"Guiding light?\nHa, what an old-fashioned relic.\nPeople use flashlights these days.\"\n\nShe wasn't unaware that it was just a metaphor; she simply scoffed at the idea.\n\nBecause one day, she would die.\nAnd after death, what reason, what mist, would remain—she would be completely liberated from this world.\n\nThat was a reasonable and inevitable conclusion.\nAll she needed to do was enjoy the process before this \"inevitability\" arrived.\n\nBut no one had ever told her that \"inevitability\" could also encounter \"unexpectedness.\"\n\nSimilar mist, similar predicaments, yet there were no mist lamps, no investigation teams, none of the familiar things.\nHer axe could sever the monsters of the world, but it could not cut through the mist born of her own loneliness and confusion.\n\nCan she go back?\nWill she go back?\nWhen can she go back...\n\nOne question after another surfaced from her heart, like an invisible deep water, slowly engulfing her soul.\nAt this moment, the only thought in her mind, the entirety of her thoughts, was—\nMaintain reason.\n\nDon't go insane!\nDon't go insane!\nDon't go insane!\n\nWhether facing the mist of that world, the mist of this world, or the mist within her heart.\n\nFor the sake of returning once more."
  },
  Item_94444_Name = {Text = "Mouchette"},
  Item_94445_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The lost consciousness of an ancient will. Mythag enlightens the consciousness of Awakeners through a mysterious ritual, and the Enlightened Awakener will gain permanent enhancements.
Convert upon obtaining duplicate Genesis: Ogier. Activates Genesis: Ogier's Enlightens.]]
  },
  Item_94445_Name = {
    Text = "Shard: Genesis: Ogier"
  },
  Item_94445_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "Convert upon obtaining duplicate Genesis: Ogier. Activates Genesis: Ogier's Enlightens."
  },
  Item_94446_Name = {
    Text = "Oath-Breaker·Ogier"
  },
  Item_94447_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with the Crit. Rate attribute."
  },
  Item_94447_Name = {
    Text = "Days Gone By Like a Shadow"
  },
  Item_94447_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "An unnamed plague devoured towns and villages, warmongers slaughtered freely amid the chaos, and a symphony of iron and blood boiled into madness.\nOut of fear, or exploiting fear.\nFear is an invisible enemy, an ancient enemy, a deadly enemy.\nHe was an unworthy knight — he had been defeated by fear.\n\nYet the vow once solemnly sworn still echoed in his ears, year after year, passing through a homeland already reduced to nothing.\n\"I shall treat the weak with mercy, I shall face the strong with courage.\"\nThe night concealed the footprints of those who did harm, floods of screams and weeping submerged the streets and alleys, the crowds like a panicked flock of sheep.\n\"I shall oppose the wicked without reservation, I shall fight for those who cannot fight.\"\nSpear tips stained with blood, silver shields eaten by rust, the shadow smiled with satisfaction, a murder of crows circled overhead, a devil's gleam flickering in their pupils.\n\"I shall help those who need my help.\"\n\"It's him, he has come.\" The people murmured in hushed voices, fear contorting their faces, \"The hollow monster, the vengeful specter, returned from the depths of death to drag his enemies into the black mire of resentment.\"\nIt was him. He had not forgotten — he had never forgotten.\n\nWhy persist? If all things must perish in the end, even glory and faith.\nWhy retreat? Since no matter how fate mocks, one can only bow and submit.\nIs it merely to be loyal to loyalty, to dedicate oneself to dedication?\nThe last knight of the Duchy asked in vain, his soul as desolate as his broken body, the lingering filth of fear flowing unchecked, converging into an ocean of destruction.\nYet the hollow chest remained silent, and the lost answer was still nowhere to be found."
  },
  Item_94448_Desc = {
    Text = "Increases the Base DMG dealt by the wielder's \"Exalt\" and \"Pursuit,\" and continuously enhance the DMG dealt by the wielder's Strike with the use of Strike cards."
  },
  Item_94448_Name = {
    Text = "Doomsday Rampage"
  },
  Item_94448_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "\"What kind of fun happens when a world is heading towards its end?\"\n\nMouchette didn't know, but she was looking forward to it.\n\nThis anticipation was different from before; this time it wasn't just about having a bit of fun with some Ancient Monsters, it was research and investigation measured on the scale of an entire world. And at the core of this research and investigation was one person—\n the Keeper of Mythag.\n\n\"I will save this world...\"\n\n\"This world will definitely not meet a fate of collapse...\"\n\nThat person, who held ideals and bore the fate of a world, made such a promise. In response, Mouchette knew she should show a moved expression; it was the social etiquette established in human society.\n\nBut she didn't want to pretend anymore, or rather, after witnessing the Keeper confront @4, sacrificing themselves to save a world, she felt there was no need to pretend in front of someone who had experienced cosmic horror.\n\n\"Pretending\" was the game rule of human society—decent yet boring—while the universe... the universe was real and straightforward—\n either survive or perish.\n\nThus, her response to the Keeper was also genuine and straightforward.\n\n\"I don't care if this world will be saved or destroyed... Compared to that, I am more curious about you.\"\n\nI am curious whether you can fulfill your ideals or if you will crumble on the path of pursuing them.\n\nI am also curious whether this world will respond to your wishes or inevitably head towards destruction.\n\nNo matter which outcome, it will be a grand and rare form of fun.\n\nI will always look forward to that day...\n\nwith my eyes and my axe, waiting."
  },
  Item_94449_Desc = {
    Text = "Amplifies the Shield and Power granted by the wielder's \"Exalt\", and provides more Shield and Power when using \"Defense\"."
  },
  Item_94449_Name = {
    Text = "And the Daisies Still Effloresce"
  },
  Item_94449_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "\"Put the wreath on properly — this is your knighting ceremony, my dear little knight.\"\nWhen daisies bloomed across the meadows, there were always idle soldiers who, under the pretense of standing guard, would drag the young boy along to wander here.\nAn ornament woven from the most common flowers of the Duchy of Aquitaine, gently placed upon golden hair.\n\"My lord, perhaps… we should be training?\"\nThe boy said this, yet obediently straightened the white flower wreath.\nThese delicate plants, always bathed in light, were also symbols of hope in the boy's homeland.\n\nWhen he opened his eyes again, those bright and vivid images were gone.\nWar horses were screaming, enemies surged forward with contempt, and amid the thousands of troops, he stood alone.\nThen, the grating clamor ceased abruptly—\nA black tide poured into his soul.\nFollowing it came the tearing sound of a spear piercing flesh, the rushing of blood, the wailing of enemies.\nThe scorn on those faces vanished without a trace, replaced by overwhelming fear and retreat.\nAnd the boy only raised his hand mechanically — thrust, withdraw, raise again.\nUntil the last soldier fell.\nDust and smoke swallowed countless faces, the remains of conquerors and conquered alike piled upon the ground, indistinguishable from one another.\n\nA shadow coiled around his spine, sneering: \"Keep going. Let your spear fall, just one more time.\"\n\"Between guardian and destroyer, there has always been only a thin line. Now, you have made your choice.\"\n\nDarkness shrouded the sky, blood soaked the earth.\nHe gazed toward the distant countryside — in just one short night, it had forever lost its former colors.\nThe wind lifted the hem of the boy's clothes, and swept across that patch of grass that had somehow survived.\nIn the silent night, in a corner unknown even to demons, a trace of pure white, barely perceptible, still lingered in the depths of his eyes.\nIt was the last daisy in this land, growing quietly in a place no one cared to notice.\nThough stained with red, its stem bent, it had not yet fallen."
  },
  Item_94559_Desc = {
    Text = "After recording this Posse, you can select the Posse Skill: \"Voracious Resolve\".\n\nThis is the Promised Land sworn by Mythag to her warriors—where jars overflow with honey and cabinets groan with meat.\nNo force may bar the brave; what is theirs by right, they shall claim."
  },
