  Item_9723_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "He was buried in the spring of @2."
  },
  Item_97242_Desc = {
    Text = "In Necrovia, death isn't feared. Instead, the days leading up to it are lived as if they were the last, filled with song, dance, feasting, and revelry—making this city of the departed far livelier than any living soul could imagine.\nWhen a purple forget-me-not drifts gently before a window, its recipient accepts this ethereal letter with grace. They bathe, groom, and don their favorite robe, fastening the flower by their temple. Bidding farewell to the city, they then take the hand of their beloved. This is a Blessing from the Lord of Necrovia, and his promise: to unite them with their loved ones, never to abandon or forget each each other. Their reunion, he promises, will last for eternity, until he himself vanishes from this world.\nNear the cemetery in the mortal realm, among those seeking liberation, a similar legend circulates. When you've suffered endlessly from worldly torments and are nearing life's end, you'll see a mist in the tranquil dawn that brings peace to the soul. Follow it into the wilderness, toward the unknown edge of the world, and you will discover a sea of purple flowers blooming among countless gravestones. At the mist's end stands a beautiful young man, as if formed from blossoms themselves, who seems to have awaited you your entire life—now simply fulfilling a fated signature, ready to guide you into a dreamland free from all agony.He will accept you, soothe your pain, and bring you final redemption.\nStanding in that sea of flowers, he will gently extend his palm and ask: \"Shall we dance?\""
  },
  Item_97242_Name = {
    Text = "Forget-Me-Not"
  },
