  },
  Item_9848_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Not a product of craftsmanship, but the tragic end of a butterfly encountering an alchemist.
A simple crystalline butterfly.
A material used for enhancing the abilities of Chaos Awakeners.]]
  },
  Item_9848_Name = {
    Text = "Faded Crystalfly"
  },
  Item_9849_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with the Aliemus Regen Level attribute."
  },
  Item_9849_Name = {
    Text = "Deathless Ascent"
  },
  Item_9849_StoryDesc = {
    Text = "They are born from humanity's imagination of the unknown, yet they do not possess the hysteria and clawing behavior often imagined.\n\nThey are rational; they are calm.\n\nThey come for the future, they come for existence.\n\nThey are the most unusual, the most incredible miracles.\n\nAt first, their voice was like the chirping of insects. But after fully comprehending their thoughts, that voice fell silent.\n\nYet afterward, the masters of the voice attempted to influence every decision she made.\n\nIn her first year as an <Awakener>, she learned to coexist with the voices in her head.\n\nShe plunged into consciousness, becoming part of the gestalt, seizing the information and knowledge she needed, and finally disengaging safely to return to reality.\n\nShe did the same when the \"Black Plague\" came for this body.\n\nShe aimed to separate the body from knowledge, memory, and soul, making the brain an immortal entity.\n\nAfter the surgery, she nearly entered a vivid and wonderful sleep—but within mere seconds, her thoughts began to operate once more.\n\nShe knew clearly that she was approaching that absolute destruction surpassing form, power, and the chaos of symmetry."
  },
  Item_9850_Desc = {
    Text = "Wheel of Destiny with the Realm Mastery attribute."
  },
  Item_9850_Name = {
    Text = "Duty's Gravitas"
  },
  Item_9850_StoryDesc = {
    Text = [[
The acting dean is an oddity on the Mythag campus.

Almost each Mythag investigator has unique abilities, while she is one of the very few with no powers beyond ordinary human limits.

Yet she holds this vital role.

Born into an ordinary family in the Elke Kingdom, she grew fierce and tenacious, shaped by local traditions.

Later, her fellow prisoner in the camp, Sophia, ignited her passion for academic research.

Her remarkable academic achievements made her the most trusted student of her mentor, the former dean of the Mythag University Biological Institute.

Thus, after her mentor disappeared, she naturally stepped in as acting dean.

Under her steadfast leadership, the institute's research continues to run smoothly.

"Fear no violence, fear no power. And so, fear no duty."]]
